WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.646
Hi, good morning, Ziad.

00:00:01.646 --> 00:00:03.077
Hope you slept okay.

00:00:03.077 --> 00:00:05.797
Today's Monday, November twenty-third.

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:11.522
A warm, breezy start to a short week, with a normal workday and one thing after.

00:00:11.522 --> 00:00:14.456
Here's one to think about while you move.

00:00:14.456 --> 00:00:20.037
When your podcast app decides an episode is new, what is it actually checking?

00:00:20.037 --> 00:00:21.469
Answer's at the end.

00:00:21.469 --> 00:00:22.471
Okay, weather.

00:00:22.471 --> 00:00:30.986
Foggy early, then partly cloudy and weirdly warm, up near the upper sixties, with gusts around twenty-five on the bike.

00:00:30.986 --> 00:00:42.222
Enjoy it, because Tuesday and Wednesday turn properly cold, and a big rain and wind storm is aimed at Thanksgiving Thursday, probably starting around midday.

00:00:42.222 --> 00:00:43.224
Okay, the day.

00:00:43.224 --> 00:00:46.444
Calendar has the gym at seven, straight sets.

00:00:46.444 --> 00:00:48.448
Then Godinger, nine to five.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:53.099
And an arts and crafts thing on there at five, for about an hour.

00:00:53.099 --> 00:00:55.103
After that the night's open.

00:00:55.103 --> 00:00:56.105
Alright, news.

00:00:56.105 --> 00:00:57.178
Closer to home.

00:00:57.178 --> 00:01:05.980
Mayor Mamdani says Rikers Island will close by twenty thirty-two, with four smaller jails in the boroughs taking its place.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:13.781
The catch is that a law from twenty nineteen already said twenty twenty-seven, and the city's behind on that.

00:01:13.781 --> 00:01:18.003
So this is kind of an honest new date more than a speed-up.

00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:21.223
The correction officers' union is against it.

00:01:21.223 --> 00:01:23.370
One from your corner, sort of.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.018
Apparently it was a bad week for A.I.

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:27.878
privacy behind the scenes.

00:01:27.878 --> 00:01:37.468
Together A.I., a company that runs open models for other apps, said someone got into stored samples of customer prompts, after an A.I.

00:01:37.468 --> 00:01:39.758
coding agent exposed a password.

00:01:39.758 --> 00:01:49.419
And OpenRouter pulled a bunch of providers off its no-data-kept list, after security researchers found prompts and keys getting stolen.

00:01:49.419 --> 00:01:56.503
So if you send work stuff through those services, that zero retention label is worth a second look.

00:01:56.503 --> 00:01:57.434
And on chips.

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:58.149
A new U.S.

00:01:58.149 --> 00:01:59.867
rule kicked in Thursday.

00:01:59.867 --> 00:02:03.373
Data centers that rent out a lot of advanced A.I.

00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:07.739
computing to Chinese companies now need a government license.

00:02:07.739 --> 00:02:12.605
Before, China could kind of rent the chips it wasn't allowed to buy.

00:02:12.605 --> 00:02:16.326
Companies already doing it get ninety days to apply.

00:02:16.326 --> 00:02:18.902
Okay, here's one for Saturday lunch.

00:02:18.902 --> 00:02:27.561
Sobre Masa is a tortilleria on Harrison Place in Bushwick, in an old warehouse, run by a chef who used to cook at Per Se.

00:02:27.561 --> 00:02:32.571
They grind their own corn, and you can see the sacks of it stacked up.

00:02:32.571 --> 00:02:38.224
Get a gringa, a cheesy, meaty taco on a fresh tortilla, about seven bucks each.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:42.160
It's a good warm stop on what should be a cold weekend.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.522
Today's challenge is a photo one.

00:02:44.522 --> 00:02:47.885
Make one picture today using only a reflection.

00:02:47.885 --> 00:02:51.749
A shop window, a car door, a puddle, a spoon at lunch.

00:02:51.749 --> 00:02:55.327
No shooting the thing itself, only its reflection.

00:02:55.327 --> 00:03:02.555
You spend all day keeping reflections out of silver, so it's kind of fun to make one the whole point.

00:03:02.555 --> 00:03:05.203
Okay, something you've been learning.

00:03:05.203 --> 00:03:08.781
Remember planning that winter trip to the Midwest?

00:03:08.781 --> 00:03:16.224
Here's why the middle of the country gets so much colder than New York, even at about the same latitude.

00:03:16.224 --> 00:03:19.372
It comes down to water being a heat battery.

00:03:19.372 --> 00:03:24.668
Water takes about four times as much energy to warm up as dry ground does.

00:03:24.668 --> 00:03:29.749
And the ocean mixes, so summer heat gets stirred down hundreds of feet.

00:03:29.749 --> 00:03:32.254
Land only warms the top few inches.

00:03:32.254 --> 00:03:40.412
So in winter, the ground gives up its heat in a few weeks, while the ocean keeps leaking summer warmth for months.

00:03:40.412 --> 00:03:45.493
That's the difference between a maritime climate and a continental one.

00:03:45.493 --> 00:03:48.283
Near a big ocean, seasons are softened.

00:03:48.283 --> 00:03:54.509
Far inland, there's nothing to cushion them, so summers get hot and winters get brutal.

00:03:54.509 --> 00:03:59.447
A typical January day in Minneapolis averages somewhere in the teens.

00:03:59.447 --> 00:04:02.238
In New York it's right around freezing.

00:04:02.238 --> 00:04:04.671
Then there's the shape of the map.

00:04:04.671 --> 00:04:11.971
The Rockies run north to south, so nothing blocks Arctic air sliding down from Canada into the Plains.

00:04:11.971 --> 00:04:13.831
It just pours straight in.

00:04:13.831 --> 00:04:15.334
And here's the twist.

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.910
New York isn't that maritime either.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:25.281
Weather here mostly moves west to east, so the air we get has usually just crossed the whole continent.

00:04:25.281 --> 00:04:33.582
That's why the Pacific Northwest, with the ocean upwind, stays so mild, and the East Coast gets real winters anyway.

00:04:33.582 --> 00:04:36.230
The Atlantic only takes the edge off.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.450
One more thing that makes it worse out there.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:43.816
Clear, dry winter nights let heat escape straight into space.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:51.688
Add snow on the ground, which bounces back sunlight during the day, and a cold snap just keeps feeding itself.

00:04:51.688 --> 00:04:57.126
So: calendar says gym at seven, Godinger till five, arts and crafts at five.

00:04:57.126 --> 00:04:59.130
Make one reflection picture.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:04.211
The answer: a permanent tag called the G.U.I.D., not the title or date.

00:05:04.211 --> 00:05:06.000
Have a good Monday, Ziad.
